        "ai_gen_block_7df23dd_8gHrti": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_7df23dd",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Most Cars Lose Their Showroom Finish",
            "heading_font": "oswald_n7",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "heading_line_height": 1.2,
            "heading_letter_spacing": 0.5,
            "heading_text_transform": "uppercase",
            "heading_color": "#ffffff",
            "heading_spacing": 20,
            "subtext": "<p>Cars don't get scratched when they get dirty.</p><p>They get scratched when you wash them.</p><p><strong>Ceramic coating changes that.</strong></p><p>Without protection, paintwork becomes:<br/></p><ul><li>Harder to clean</li><li>More prone to swirl marks</li><li>Vulnerable to permanent water spot damage</li><li>Paint becomes dull from sun damage</li><li>Prone to paint bubbling and rust</li><li>Increasingly difficult to maintain<br/></li></ul><p>Over time, correcting these issues becomes significantly more expensive or even impossible, compared to preventing them in the first place.</p>",
